<!--
  One <recording> element, matching (field-for-field) the OFFICIAL documented example response
  for BigBlueButton's GET getRecordings API call - see
  https://docs.bigbluebutton.org/development/api/#get-getrecordings (fetched and verified live
  against that page - not from memory). Values below are that page's own example values, not
  fabricated. In production this lane would call getRecordings for one meeting and land the
  single <recording> block it gets back for that meeting, in this same shape.

  Honesty note (unchanged from before): <participants> here is a COUNT ("3"), not a per-person
  list - BBB's public, documented API has no per-participant join/leave endpoint. The only place
  BBB exposes that is "Learning Analytics Dashboard" data, which is either an INTERNAL,
  undocumented API call (learningDashboard, listed under "Internal API calls" in BBB's own
  docs - not part of the public developer-facing surface) or a server-to-server callback
  (meta_analytics-callback-url, pushed by the BBB server when a meeting ends) - neither is a
  regular API call this lane could make the way it calls getRecordings. So participants stays
  empty in MeetingMetadata for BBB - there is genuinely nothing to parse here, not a gap in our
  parsing.
-->
